<article class="env-lemma" id="05AF">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/05AF">Lemma <span data-tag="05AF">31.2.5</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a locally Noetherian scheme. Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then $\text{Ass}(\mathcal{F}) \cap U$ is finite for every quasi-compact open $U \subset X$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because the set of associated primes of a finite module over a Noetherian ring is finite, see Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/00LC" data-tag="00LC">10.63.5</a>. To translate from schemes to algebra use that $U$ is a finite union of affine opens, each of these opens is the spectrum of a Noetherian ring (Properties, Lemma <a href="/tag/01OW" data-tag="01OW">28.5.2</a>), $\mathcal{F}$ corresponds to a finite module over this ring (Cohomology of Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01XZ" data-tag="01XZ">30.9.1</a>), and finally use Lemma <a href="/tag/02OK" data-tag="02OK">31.2.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>